      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2015, Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Transradial coronary angiography (TRC) can be performed applying only one catheter fitting into the right and left coronary ostia (R/LCO). In this bicentric study (n\u2009=\u20092953), we analyzed the ostial performance of the Tiger_II_catheter widely used in TRC. Compared to Judkins catheters, the Tiger_II is frequently associated with ostial instability within the LCO but fits better into the RCO-irrespective of tube size. Judkins catheters generally need more peri-procedural contrast and radiation exposure. TRC may be started using a 5F_Tiger_II on the right side in order to be switched to 5F Judkins in case of propable LCO instability."
      },
